The road continued east. The sun climbed behind us. The forest opened and closed around the road like breathing   dense stands of old growth giving way to meadows that gave way to more forest. The sky was clear and wide and indifferent. The temperature was cool and the air was clean and I was walking through a beautiful world in a body that was becoming something beautiful itself, whether I wanted it or not.

